<title>USA: Cherokee signs licensing pact.</title>
<headline>Cherokee signs licensing pact.</headline>
<dateline>VAN NUYS, Calif. 1997-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cherokee Inc on Monday said it has signed a master licensing agreement with Kumkyung Co Ltd to further develop Cherokee's family apparel, fashion accessories, home textiles and other products in South Korea.</p>
<p>Kumkyung is a retailer and apparel maker with operations in Korea, China, the United States and Nicaragua. Its president, Paul Lee, developed the Christian Dior and Girbaud brands in South Korea, Cherokee said in a statement.</p>
</text>
